            <ArticleTitle>Left internal thoracic artery harvesting: measurement of the length required for coronary bypass surgery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1160-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1510/icvts.2008.189100</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The left internal thoracic artery (LITA) is used routinely for coronary bypass surgery. A simple technique for assessing, prior to harvesting, the length of LITA required for an individual bypass of the left anterior descending artery (LAD) is described.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
